hi this is presh talwalkar let's discuss  math problems where people are working  together to do a job the 1994 movie  little big league features one of these  problems  joe can paint a house in three hours  and his friend sam can paint the same  house in five hours how long will it  take if they paint the house together  the players come up with several wrong  answers by combining the numbers 3 and  5.  the most plausible answer is the average  of 4 hours  but this is clearly wrong because of  joke and paint house in three hours it  has to take them less than three hours  working together  the correct answer one of the players  gets to is one and seven eighths hour  but how did he get to this answer  we need to look at the rate of work  if joe can paint the house in three  hours then every hour he paints a third  of the house  which means he paints x over three of  the house in x hours  similarly sam will paint x over five of  the house in x hours  working together we add the rates of  work to get x over three plus x over  five equals one hundred percent  we can easily solve this equation to get  1 and 7 8 hour  more generally  we can think about people working at  different rates  and we can consider the time it takes  them to complete the job working  together the formula is a times b over a  plus b  please subscribe to my channel i make  videos on math and game theory you can  support me on patreon catch me on my  blog find your decisions  on twitter at preshellwalker and you can  get my books at amazon
 

